 r←Test_UC_303(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;project;parms;success;log;ref;rc;msg;res;buff
⍝ Call ]Cider.CloseProject without an argument while more than one project is open, and quit with "q".
⍝ `UC.CloseProject` used to crash with an INDEX ERROR on the ¯1 that CommTools 3 returns for "q".
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 ⍝ Automating "q" requires CommTools 3.0.1 or later; without it this test would prove nothing
 ref←∆GetRefToCommTools
 ref.AddAutomation'Select' 'CheckQ@' 'q'
 buff←'CheckQ@Check:'ref.Select,¨'a' 'b'
 ref.Cleanup
 'CommTools automation does not return ¯1 for "q"'Assert ¯1≡buff

 #.⎕EX¨'TEMP' 'TEMP2'
 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 'TEMP2'#.⎕NS''
 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)('IfExists' 'Replace')⊢##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/Tests/Test_Alias/*'
 ref.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'ChangeCurrentDir@' 'n'
 :For project :In 'Project1' 'Project2'
     parms←##.Cider.CreateOpenParms ⍬
     parms.folder←tempDir,'/',project
     parms.watch←'ns'
     parms.ignoreUserExec←1
     parms.batch←1
     (success log)←##.Cider.OpenProject parms
     →T.GoToTidyUp~success
 :EndFor

 ref.AddAutomation'Select' 'Select Cider project(s) to be closed' 'q'
 (rc msg res)←∆UCMD'CloseProject'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Cancelled by user'⍷res
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∧/'#.TEMP' '#.TEMP2'∊{⍵[;1]}##.Cider.ListOpenProjects 0   ⍝ Nothing got closed

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ref.Cleanup
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break'#.TEMP'
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break'#.TEMP2'
 #.⎕EX¨'TEMP' 'TEMP2'
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert 0=rc
⍝Done
